WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.502
In 1936, Inge Lehmann noticed faint
waves arriving where none should, and

00:00:05.502 --> 00:00:08.566
worked out that the core has a solid
heart.

00:00:09.016 --> 00:00:13.649
The inner core begins 5,150 km down.

00:00:14.099 --> 00:00:19.044
It is iron at more than 4,000 °C,
kept solid by the pressure.

00:00:19.494 --> 00:00:26.584
At the centre, 6,371 km down, the
pressure is 3.6 million times that of

00:00:26.584 --> 00:00:28.481
the air around you.

00:00:28.931 --> 00:00:33.475
Waves that cross the inner core from
pole to pole arrive a few seconds

00:00:33.475 --> 00:00:33.865
early.

00:00:34.315 --> 00:00:37.635
Its iron has a grain, and nobody yet
knows why.
